course: dictionary
lesson: 15244
title: Sherry, a grown-up word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Sherry is a noun, a thing you can name. It is a strong wine from Spain, and it is for grown-ups, not children. Context helps you see this. «Grandma adds a splash of sherry to the trifle.» Sherry is something you add to a pudding, so it is a food or drink, not a fruit or a cake.
explain: «The adults raised a glass of sherry at the Christmas party.» Here sherry means the drink itself. A glass of sherry is one glass full of it. The word «sherry» can also be used on its own to mean one glass, as in «A sherry, please», but this is for adults only.
explain: Sherry is strong, so it is not a drink for children. Children have lemonade or juice at parties instead. When you meet a new word, ask yourself what it does in the sentence, and whether a grown-up or a child would use it.
fact: Sherry is a strong wine from Spain.
fact: Sherry is often drunk in a small glass.
fact: Sherry is sometimes used in cooking, for example in trifle.
fact: Sherry is alcohol, so it is only for adults. Children must never drink it.
fact: Phrases with sherry include «a glass of sherry», «sweet sherry» and «dry sherry».
exercise: «Grandma adds a splash of sherry to the trifle.» What is sherry? | A cake with cream on top | A small green fruit | A type of lemonade | *A strong wine from Spain
exercise: Where does sherry come from? | France | Scotland | Australia | *Spain
exercise: Who is sherry for? | Children at every party | *Only grown-ups | Dogs | Babies
test: «The adults raised a glass of sherry at the Christmas party.» In this sentence, what does sherry mean? | A party game | A school bag | *The drink itself, or one glass of it | A type of Christmas tree
test: Which phrase is a sherry phrase? | dry toast | warm milk | *dry sherry | sweet bread
exam: «Sherry is for grown-ups only, so children drink lemonade.» Why is sherry not for children? | Because it is too sweet to drink | Because it comes from a shop | Because it is cold | *Because it is alcohol
